@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Octo 17: signals, images and sound)

Signal processing works on vectors of samples; images are matrices of pixels.

@section(Spectra)

`fft` turns samples into frequencies; `fftshift` centres zero frequency.

@octo
fs = 100; t = (0:fs-1) / fs;
x = sin(2*pi*5*t) + 0.5 * sin(2*pi*20*t);
X = abs(fft(x)) / numel(x);
[~, k] = sort(X(1:50), "descend"); sort(k(1:2) - 1)
real(ifft(fft([1 2 3])))
fftshift(1:4)
plot(0:49, X(1:50)); title("amplitude spectrum"); xlabel("Hz");
@end

@section(Filters)

`filter` applies a difference equation; `butter` designs a filter; `freqz` shows its response.

@octo
y = filter(ones(1, 3) / 3, 1, [3 6 9 12 15])
[b, a] = butter(2, 0.2);
round(b * 1e4) / 1e4
[H, w] = freqz(b, a, 64); figure; plot(w / pi, abs(H)); title("Butterworth response");
conv([1 2], [1 3]), xcorr([1 2 3])
hamming(4)', hann(4)'
@end

@section(Spectral estimates)

`periodogram` and `pwelch` estimate the power at each frequency.

@octo
t = (0:255) / 64; x = sin(2*pi*8*t) + 0.2 * randn(size(t));
[p, f] = periodogram(x, [], [], 64); [~, i] = max(p); f(i)
[pw, fw] = pwelch(x, [], [], [], 64); numel(pw) > 0
@end

@section(Images)

An image is a matrix; `imagesc` and `image` show it, `conv2` blurs it with a kernel.

@octo
I = peaks(40);
imagesc(I); colormap(gray); axis image; title("an image is a matrix");
B = conv2(I, ones(3) / 9, "same"); size(B)
figure; image(uint8(rand(8, 8, 3) * 255)); title("an RGB image");
G = rgb2gray(rand(4, 4, 3)); size(G)
@end

@section(Sound)

`sound(y, fs)` plays a vector of samples at fs samples per second; the reader presses play.

@octo
fs = 8000; t = (0:fs-1) / fs;
y = 0.5 * sin(2*pi*440*t) .* exp(-3*t);
sound(y, fs)
@end
